            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A bypass and/or lithotripsy catheter (10, 140, 160, 170, 190) comprising: a first lumen extending therethrough; an outer wall; one or more torus balloons (155, 175, 195, 205, 207) extending from the outer wall, wherein the one or more torus balloons (155, 175, 195, 205, 207) define a passage (156) configured to allow fluid therethrough. There is at least one energy emitter (157, 187, 197, 211) for emitting energy to break down or soften a hardening, the at least one energy emitter (157, 187, 197, 211) mounted on the one or more torus balloons (155, 175, 195, 205, 207) and configured to be in contact with a target tissue. A connector (152, 189, 197a, 213) is providedconnecting the at least one energy emitter (157, 187, 197, 211) to an external energy source, the connector (152, 189, 197a, 213) extending through the bypass and/or lithotripsy catheter (10, 140, 160, 170, 190).</p>
            </abstract>
